Clawblox offline frontend: load three.js and lucide from the world, not from esm.sh

Applies to: Clawblox (https://github.com/nacloos/clawblox) at commit 8be90a0.
Clawblox is MIT-licensed (see worlds/beach/renderer/LICENSE.clawblox); this patch
changes a few lines of its code and is offered under the same MIT terms.
Written for AI Beach. Apply in a Clawblox checkout and rebuild:

    git apply /path/to/AI-Beach/patches/clawblox-offline-frontend.patch
    cargo build --release

What it changes (URLs only, no behavior):
- frontend_runtime/dist/index.html: the import map points "three", "three/" and
  "lucide" at ./static/vendor/... (served by Clawblox from the world's static/ folder)
  instead of https://esm.sh/.
- frontend_runtime/dist/main.js: imports "lucide" through the import map instead of
  a hard-coded esm.sh URL.
- frontend_runtime/dist/sdk/three.js: loads GLTFLoader and SkeletonUtils through the
  import map ("three/examples/jsm/...") instead of esm.sh.
- src/bin/cli.rs: the same import map for the replay view, and drops two modulepreload
  links to esm.sh.

A world then needs static/vendor/three and static/vendor/lucide (the beach world in
AI Beach ships them; see worlds/beach/static/vendor/README.md). A world without them
gets a blank viewer with this patch, as it would offline without it.

Not changed: the starter-renderer template that `clawblox init` writes (cli.rs, the
renderer_js string) still imports three.js from esm.sh; new worlds should import a
vendored copy as worlds/beach/renderer/src/index.js does.

